		{
			description: [
				"Turbines eat the steam of the column to their left. A boiler that keeps up with them is the real limit."
				""
				"EU per bucket, from the recipes in this pack:"
				"&6Steam&r: 500 EU"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:steam_bucket"
			id: "6825BD9BBB0C7299"
			optional: true
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "square"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "Steam, and nothing else."
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "260AE1B86DE3F790"
					type: "checkmark"
					title: "Read"
				}
			]
			title: "What Steam Turbines Burn"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Combustion Generators burn liquid fuels. The cheapest ones, &6Ethanol&r and &6Biodiesel&r, need no oil at all."
				""
				"EU per bucket, from the recipes in this pack:"
				"&6High Octane Gasoline&r: 3,200,000 EU"
				"&6Gasoline&r: 1,600,000 EU"
				"&6Cetane Boosted Diesel&r: 720,000 EU"
				"&6Diesel&r: 480,000 EU"
				"&6Toluene&r: 320,000 EU"
				"&6Naphtha&r: 320,000 EU"
				"&6Light Fuel&r: 320,000 EU"
				"&6Bio Diesel&r: 256,000 EU"
				"&6Rocket Fuel&r: 250,000 EU"
				"&6Ethanol&r: 192,000 EU"
				"&6Octane&r: 80,000 EU"
				"&6Methanol&r: 64,000 EU"
				"...and 3 more; the recipe viewer lists them all."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:diesel_bucket"
			id: "245DCFF675F471FD"
			optional: true
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "square"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "Liquid fuels, best first."
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "1EEFF7F4F64B6DC7"
					type: "checkmark"
					title: "Read"
				}
			]
			title: "What Combustion Burns"
			x: 6.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Gas Turbines burn gases and light hydrocarbons. Several of them come out of the same distillation that makes combustion fuel, so the two columns grow together."
				""
				"EU per bucket, from the recipes in this pack:"
				"&6Nitrobenzene&r: 1,280,000 EU"
				"&6Benzene&r: 352,000 EU"
				"&6Lpg&r: 320,000 EU"
				"&6Butane&r: 296,000 EU"
				"&6Phenol&r: 288,000 EU"
				"&6Butene&r: 256,000 EU"
				"&6Propane&r: 232,000 EU"
				"&6Butadiene&r: 204,000 EU"
				"&6Propene&r: 192,000 EU"
				"&6Ethane&r: 168,000 EU"
				"&6Refinery Gas&r: 160,000 EU"
				"&6Ethylene&r: 128,000 EU"
				"...and 6 more; the recipe viewer lists them all."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:methane_bucket"
			id: "6888AA3D8B43F8F1"
			optional: true
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "square"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "Gases, best first."
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4406E1DAF565FD1B"
					type: "checkmark"
					title: "Read"
				}
			]
			title: "What Gas Turbines Burn"
			x: 8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Boilers burn fuel and turn &6Water&r into &6Steam&r. They make no EU themselves: the turbines of the next column do."
				""
				"&aCount your boilers first. A turbine is only as good as the steam behind it.&r"
